      "content": "Apologies for the oversight. Upon re-examination, Patent Number US9421732 does indeed raise concerns for the novelty of NexaCore's proposal. This patent involves a modular battery cooling interface that shares several similarities with NexaCore's concept. It outlines a system where modular components—including cooling—are used in conjunction with solid-state technology.\n\nHowever, US9421732 does not seem to address the unique aspects of NexaCore's system, especially the usage of a recyclable cooling medium and the direct integration of thermal management feedback within the battery modules. Additionally, NexaCore's claims also focus on an adaptive cooling mechanism that adjusts in real-time to battery performance, which is not covered by US9421732.\n\nDespite the similarities, it seems NexaCore's unique combination of these elements offers an inventive step that the US9421732 patent is unlikely to preempt. However, I would strongly recommend that we consider how closely we may tread and perhaps adjust our claims to further distance from US9421732 or argue for the inventive step in our technology when drafting the final application. It will be crucial to describe the differences clearly to the examiners and potentially provide a robust argument that NexaCore's innovative aspects are not anticipated by US942",
